      "game_seq": 334,
      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "It looks like the opponent sacrificed North Pole Gates to Momo on turn 6, drawing a card and leaving them with 1 card in hand. On my turn 7 with 6 mana available, I'm weighing playing Messenger Hawk plus cracking a Clue, versus Hawk with Mechanist animating a Clue into a 3/1 flier to attack.\n\
\n\
Since my current Teo has Path to Redemption attached and can't attack or block, casting a second Teo triggers the legend rule — but I can choose to keep the new one and let the old Pathed copy die, effectively removing the Path lockdown for 4 mana. That leaves 2 mana to either crack a Clue or animate one with Mechanist to swing alongside Jailer; I'm considering how Momo (1/1 flying vigilance, summoning sick but able to block) would trade against either the 3/3 Jailer or the 3/1 flying construct, and whether trading my Clue token for Momo is a reasonable exchange.\n\
\n\
Casting the new Teo triggers its flying-attack loot ability even though it's summoning sick, since the trigger just needs a flyer attacking. My plan: play the land, cast Teo #2 letting the Pathed one die, then animate the Clue and swing with Jailer plus the construct to get the loot trigger, accepting the risk that the opponent's six open lands and one card could hold a flash blocker. Getting Path off Teo feels like the clear value play over just cracking the Clue for a card.\n\
\n\
